# client/ and server/ each carry their own .gitignore, because either project can
# be cloned and worked on without this file being present. This one covers only
# what sits at the top level, plus a safety net for the things that must never
# be committed no matter where in the tree they appear.

node_modules/
dist/
.next/
test-results/
playwright-report/

.DS_Store
*.log

# Never commit a real env file from anywhere in the tree.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Templates carry no values, only the shape of the file and why each line is
# there, so they belong in the repo like .env.example does.
!.env.production.example

# Installed agent skills. These come from an upstream toolkit rather than from
# this project, are refreshed by their own installer, and would otherwise put
# ninety files of somebody else's prose into every diff.
.claude/skills/
.agents/skills/

# Database dumps. Local copies of everything the product holds — never in git.
backups/

# Personal operating notes: what to revisit and at roughly what scale. Written
# for one reader, revised constantly, and full of judgement calls that would
# read as commitments if they were in the repository's history.
FUTURE-CHECKS.md
